  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.8.12 - on SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.4.25. CUDA prefill: F16 weights now run on the tensor cores with split activations (A = hi + lo * 2^-11, so the activations are not rounded to f16): qwen3:1.7b Q4_K_M prefill ~8.0k -> ~9.85k tok/s at 1,830 tokens (+23%), greedy text identical. NEW OPT-IN (off by default, env GGUF_INT8_ACT=1 or FusedDequantMatMul.Int8ActGemv): Ollama's int8-activation decode (ggml q8_1 + dp4a) for Q4_K and Q6_K GEMVs, with the quantize fused into the norm, SwiGLU and attention merge: decode ~237 -> ~261 tok/s short, ~222 -> ~242 long on an RTX 4070, at a measured cost of KL 5.5e-3 / top-1 96.4% / perplexity +1.1% against the default (the kernels compute ggml's scheme to 1e-8). The default stays fp32 activations. See CHANGELOG.md.",
